{"text": "measurable", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Old French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">mesurable</i>, equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">measure</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-able</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Adjective", "definitions": [{"definition": "Able to be measured.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "Of significant importance.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}, {"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "That which can be measured; a metric.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["IPA", "/\u02c8m\u025b\u0292\u0259\u0279\u0259b\u0259l/"]]}